WEBVTT

00:00.200 --> 00:03.900
Moving your files out of Dropbox or OneDrive?

00:04.200 --> 00:07.500
The usual ways send your files through someone else’s servers,

00:07.700 --> 00:11.100
or fill up your computer first.

00:11.300 --> 00:14.800
Stop halfway, and you’re left hunting for what’s missing.

00:15.600 --> 00:19.500
NexMove takes the straight line.

00:21.400 --> 00:26.000
Pick your move — from Dropbox or Microsoft OneDrive, to Google Drive or OneDrive.

00:26.300 --> 00:28.900
Sign in to Dropbox.

00:29.400 --> 00:31.600
Sign in to Google.

00:32.100 --> 00:33.800
Press Start copying.

00:34.000 --> 00:37.900
Your files go from Dropbox, through your own PC, into Google Drive.

00:38.600 --> 00:42.600
No servers in between — not ours, not anyone’s.

00:43.200 --> 00:47.200
Nothing is saved to your hard drive.

00:47.600 --> 00:51.900
And if it stops, press Start again. It copies only what’s left.

00:52.300 --> 00:59.700
When it’s done, every file is checked against the original — so you can cancel your old plan with confidence.

01:00.400 --> 01:05.000
NexMove, by K-NEX. One app, three moves. Pay once. Coming soon for Windows.
